save(371,dict(paragraphs=["Ketaki Mazumdar is a poet and educationist based in Mumbai, with childhood roots in Kolkata. Her poetry collections include Woodsmoke and Embers and Toasted Orange Embers. In an interview with The Wise Owl, she describes resilience, empathy and healing as concerns that draw her poems together, and close observation of colour and movement as part of her writing practice.","In Kabita Live’s ‘Holding On Letting Go’, grief and uncertainty are met through small acts of attention: flowering trees, an earthen lamp, a river and birdsong. The poem moves between vulnerability and wonder, finding renewal without pretending that loss has disappeared."],sources=[source('Ukiyoto — Ketaki Mazumdar','https://www.ukiyoto.com/literary-awards/ketaki-mazumdar',['Mumbai and Kolkata connections; educationist; collection titles']),source('The Wise Owl — Talking Books with Ketaki Mazumdar','https://editor2733.wixsite.com/website-4/talking-books-ketaki-mazumdar',['First-person account of resilience, empathy, healing and visual observation; Toasted Orange Embers'])],books=[dict(title='Toasted Orange Embers',detail='Poetry · author interview in The Wise Owl',url='https://editor2733.wixsite.com/website-4/talking-books-ketaki-mazumdar')],identity_match='Name, educationist background, Mumbai/Kolkata connections and nature/spirituality concerns agree with the captured biography.',poems_read=[dict(id=480,title='Holding On Letting Go',basis='Read in full: grief, vulnerability, flowering trees, lamp, river, birdsong and renewed wonder.')],limitations=['Ukiyoto teaching-award account pairs 2001 with President A.P.J. Abdul Kalam; chronology unresolved and award omitted.','Poet-of-the-Year dates differ across source accounts; awards omitted.','Wise Owl page includes unrelated interview content below the Ketaki interview; only the named interview used.'],next_action='Independent author/editor review of narrative; resolve award chronology only if awards are later included.'))
